<article class="env-remark" id="823C34">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/823C34">Remark <span data-tag="823C34">8.3.2.3</span>.</a> Suppose that the collection of weak equivalences in $\mathbf{S}$ is stable under filtered colimits. Then it is easy to see that the collection of weak equivalences in $\SCat $ is also stable under filtered colimits. If $\mathbf{S}$ is also a combinatorial model category, then a bit more effort shows that the class of weak equivalences in $\SCat $ is perfect, in the sense of Definition <a href="/tag/7E81CB" data-tag="7E81CB">8.2.6.10</a>. </p>
</article>